TITLE:: PltRecurrence
summary:: Self-similarity of a sound, under one metric or two
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltObservers, Classes/PltNovelty

DESCRIPTION::
Every moment of a sound against every other, bright where they are alike. Blocks
along the diagonal are sections; bright patches away from it are returns.

Given two metrics, the square is split on its diagonal, one below and one above. The
same sound then shows two forms, and the caption gives the rank correlation between
them. Distances are ranked before drawing, so both halves spend the same brightness
and differ only in where they put it.

A metric is code::\mfcc:: (coefficients 1 to 12 of 40 mel bands, leaving out the
0th as link::Classes/MFCC:: does), code::\mel:: (the band levels in dB), or an Array
of link::Classes/PltObservers#*describe:: names, each z-scored over the file.

